<title>BELGIUM: EP approves ship safety standard report.</title>
<headline>EP approves ship safety standard report.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plans to improve safety standards on passenger ships operating on domestic routes were approved by the European Parliament on Thursday.</p>
<p>MEPs adopted a report by Swedish Christian Democrat Per Stenmarck which approves a European Commission proposal to to replace EU member states' widely differing safety rules for such vessels by harmonised European standards - COM(96)61.</p>
<p>Passenger ships on domestic routes are not covered by the international safety requirements laid down by the International Maritime Organisation, even though they are exposed to the same dangers as ships on international routes sailing in the same areas.</p>
<p>(See also Wednesday's BC-PARLIAMENT-SHIPS)</p>
</text>
